Index: Workflow

Purpose:
  The .sdd system's workflow engine entry point — SDLC + STLC
   integrating engine. This file defines how workflow will be applied,
   which files will be read in what order, and how workflow connects to
   other .sdd components.

  Workflow combines two engines:
    SDLC — software development lifecycle (AN > AR > DB > BE > API >
           FE > MD > QA > SC > DO > VR)
    STLC — software testing lifecycle (T0 > T1 > T2 > T3 > T4 > T5 >
           T6 > T7)


Owns:
  ./

Scope:
  Stage registry
  Stage transitions
  Gate criteria
  Test levels
  State machine
  Task queue engine
  Runtime events


DoesNotOwn:
  Project-specific flows (bax project/flows.sdd)
  Project-specific chains (bax chains/chains.sdd)
  Engineering skills (bax skills/)
  Task instances (bax tasks/)
  Project architecture (bax project/architecture.sdd)


ReadOrder:
  1  @./stages.sdd        — formal stage registry
  2  @./transitions.sdd   — default and conditional transitions
  3  @./gates.sdd         — gate criteria for each stage
  4  @./testing.sdd       — test levels T0-T7, test pyramid
  5  @./state.sdd         — task state machine (STATE, not STAGE)
  6  @../runtime/events.sdd — runtime event log format


Navigation:
  Stages:      @./stages.sdd
  Transitions: @./transitions.sdd
  Gates:       @./gates.sdd
  Testing:     @./testing.sdd
  State:       @./state.sdd
  Events:      @../runtime/events.sdd
  Chains:      @../chains/
  Tasks:       @../tasks/
  Skills:      @../skills/
  State:       @../state/state.sdd


Rules:

  [W1]  AI MUST load workflow/INDEX.sdd before reading any workflow
        component — never read workflow files blindly.

  [W2]  A stage MUST be declared in stages.sdd before it can appear in
        any chain or transition.

  [W3]  A transition MUST reference valid source and target stages.

  [W4]  A gate MUST declare pass/fail criteria before the stage can
        advance.

  [W5]  State (workflow/state.sdd) and Stage (stages.sdd) are distinct
        concepts — a task at stage BE may be in state BLOCKED.

  [W6]  A task MUST NOT advance past a gate without passing it.

  [W7]  Test levels (T0-T7) are independent of stages — a stage MAY
        activate multiple test levels.

  [W8]  The task queue engine (NextAction) operates on task state, not
        stage — next valid transition determines next action.

  [W9]  Runtime events (events.sdd) MUST be appended, never modified —
        history is append-only.

  [W10] A workflow change (new stage, new transition, new gate) requires
        human approval if it affects an existing project's chains.


State: +
  